Hi Silvia,

Typically, each band on a RAPD gel is a dominant locus just as in AFLP scored as o and 1 for absence and presence. Homozygous (with two copies) is close to impossible to score.  Loci found for each primer combination can be concatenated into one large genotype sheet.

Best,

Nik

