 I am Master's student working a thesis looking at gene-flow and populations structure of Brook Trout. Most of the literature in the world of Brook Trout genetics uses GENEPOP to look for linkage-disequilibrium between loci. When I run an LD test in GENEPOP I get relatively high P values (almost all >.05) however when I run the Index of Association test for LD in poppr, all but 2 of my populations had P=.001 suggesting significant LD is occuring. I know a bonferonni correction is sometimes used to correct for multiple tests, but I'm not sure this is appropriate in the case of the Index of Association. Any info you have would be appreciated.

